# 20. Key Lesson

Today's main lesson was that **IT Support troubleshooting should be based on evidence rather than assumptions**.

For example, if a user reports a slow computer, I should not immediately close applications or restart services. I should first gather information, examine system resources, identify the abnormal behavior, make an appropriate and authorized change, verify the result, and document the resolution.

The same principle applies to Active Directory and networking:

```text
Understand the symptom
        ↓
Gather information
        ↓
Investigate
        ↓
Identify likely cause
        ↓
Apply controlled fix
        ↓
Verify
        ↓
Document
        ↓
Escalate when necessary
```

